=== EXTENDED-n FOLLOW-UP (self-caught, see ATTEMPT.md Sec 8) ===
The MAIN GRID above shows the leading-order log-log slope drifting
visibly below the predicted -0.5 at larger lambda (e.g. lambda=3.0:
-0.41 to -0.43 over n in [1e4,2.56e6]), and the corrected slope
correspondingly short of -1. Investigated directly, not dismissed:
pushing n further (to 1e9) at three representative (lambda,gamma)
points below shows the LOCAL slope converging cleanly to -0.5 and
-1.0 respectively as n grows -- i.e. this is a genuine pre-asymptotic
finite-n effect (larger lambda needs larger n to reach the claimed
asymptotic rate, since c(lambda,gamma)=1/(12 lambda) is itself
smaller at large lambda, so higher-order terms remain relatively
more significant longer), not a flaw in the derived rate itself.

