=== SUMMARY ===
If, at every (lambda,gamma) in the MAIN GRID, the leading-order slope
is close to -0.5 and the corrected slope is close to -1 (or steeper),
this confirms the claimed uniform O(1/sqrt(n)) remainder for the
leading Laplace approx and that Delta genuinely captures the next
order, UNIFORMLY across the tested lambda range. If lambda=0.05
(outside the claimed range) shows visibly larger Delta / less clean
improvement from correction, this substantiates -- not just asserts
-- that lambda bounded away from 0 is a genuine, necessary condition
